§§ `Section 20: inflicting bodily injury, with or without weapon`

-- src:28 | 20 Inflicting bodily injury, with or without weapon.
-- src:29 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously wound or inflict any grievous bodily harm upon any other person, either with or without any weapon or instrument, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 20 (src:28-29)
-- "wound or inflict any grievous bodily harm upon any other person, either with or
-- without any weapon or instrument": the weapon is not an element.  Section 18 says
-- "cause" and this section says "inflict"; the encoding keeps the two verbs in two
-- fields and does not decide whether they differ in meaning.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 20` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wounded another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inflicted grievous bodily harm upon another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used a weapon or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 20 (src:29)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 20`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND (   c's `wounded another person`
         OR c's `inflicted grievous bodily harm upon another person`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 20 (src:29)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 20: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

-- "liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude . . .": the dots stand where the term
-- was; the text as deposited does not state it.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 20 (src:29)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 20: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 21: attempting to choke, &c. in order to commit any indictable offence`

-- src:30 | 21 Attempting to choke, &c. in order to commit any indictable offence.
-- src:31 | Whosoever shall, by any means whatsoever, attempt to choke, suffocate, or strangle any other person, or shall by any means calculated to choke, suffocate, or strangle, attempt to render any other person insensible, unconscious, or incapable of resistance, with intent in any of such cases thereby to enable himself or any other person to commit, or with intent in any of such cases thereby to assist any other person in committing, any indictable offence, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude for life . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 21 (src:30-31)
-- Two attempts: (1) "by any means whatsoever, attempt to choke, suffocate, or strangle
-- any other person"; (2) "by any means calculated to choke, suffocate, or strangle,
-- attempt to render any other person insensible, unconscious, or incapable of
-- resistance".  Plus an intent, either of two: to enable themselves or any other
-- person to commit, or to assist any other person in committing, any indictable
-- offence.  The text does not use "unlawfully" or "maliciously" here.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 21` HAS
    `attempted to choke, suffocate or strangle another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attempted, by means calculated to choke, suffocate or strangle, to render another person insensible, unconscious or incapable of resistance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended thereby to enable themselves or another person to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended thereby to assist another person in committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 21 (src:31)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 21`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` c MEANS
        (   c's `attempted to choke, suffocate or strangle another person`
         OR c's `attempted, by means calculated to choke, suffocate or strangle, to render another person insensible, unconscious or incapable of resistance`)
    AND (   c's `intended thereby to enable themselves or another person to commit an indictable offence`
         OR c's `intended thereby to assist another person in committing an indictable offence`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 21 (src:31)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 21: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 21 (src:31)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 21: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 22: using chloroform, &c. to commit any indictable offence`

-- src:32 | 22 Using chloroform, &c. to commit any indictable offence.
-- src:33 | Whosoever shall unlawfully apply or administer to or cause to be taken by, or attempt to apply or administer to or attempt to cause to be administered to or taken by, any person, any chloroform, laudanum, or other stupefying or overpowering drug, matter, or thing, with intent in any of such cases thereby to enable himself or any other person to commit, or with intent in any of such cases thereby to assist any other person in committing, any indictable offence, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude for life . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 22 (src:32-33)
-- "apply or administer to or cause to be taken by, or attempt to apply or administer
-- to or attempt to cause to be administered to or taken by, any person, any
-- chloroform, laudanum, or other stupefying or overpowering drug, matter, or thing":
-- doing it, or attempting to.  "Unlawfully" is in the text; "maliciously" is not.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 22` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied or administered to a person, or caused to be taken by a person, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attempted to apply or administer to a person, or to cause to be taken by a person, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended thereby to enable themselves or another person to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended thereby to assist another person in committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 22 (src:33)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 22`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND (   c's `applied or administered to a person, or caused to be taken by a person, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing`
         OR c's `attempted to apply or administer to a person, or to cause to be taken by a person, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing`)
    AND (   c's `intended thereby to enable themselves or another person to commit an indictable offence`
         OR c's `intended thereby to assist another person in committing an indictable offence`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 22 (src:33)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 22: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 22 (src:33)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 22: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 23: maliciously administering poison, &c. so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm`

-- src:34 | 23 Maliciously administering poison, &c. so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm.
-- src:35 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously administer to or cause to be administered to or taken by any other person any poison or other destructive or noxious thing, so as thereby to endanger the life of such person, or so as thereby to inflict upon such person any grievous bodily harm, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude for any term not exceeding ten years . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 23 (src:34-35)
-- The result is an element: the thing administered must "thereby" endanger the life of
-- the person or inflict grievous bodily harm on them.  No ulterior intent is required.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 23` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `administered to another person, or caused to be administered to or taken by another person, a poison or other destructive or noxious thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `thereby endangered the life of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `thereby inflicted grievous bodily harm upon that person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 23 (src:35)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 23`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND c's `administered to another person, or caused to be administered to or taken by another person, a poison or other destructive or noxious thing`
    AND (   c's `thereby endangered the life of that person`
         OR c's `thereby inflicted grievous bodily harm upon that person`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 23 (src:35)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 23: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

-- "penal servitude for any term not exceeding ten years": 120 months.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 23 (src:35)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 23: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 120)

§§ `Section 24: maliciously administering poison, &c. with intent to injure, aggrieve, or annoy any other person`

-- src:36 | 24 Maliciously administering poison, &c. with intent to injure, aggrieve, or annoy any other person.
-- src:37 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously administer to or cause to be administered to or taken by any other person any poison or other destructive or noxious thing, with intent to injure, aggrieve, or annoy such person, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 24 (src:36-37)
-- The same administering as section 23, but with an intent (to injure, aggrieve or
-- annoy) in place of a result.  "aggrieve" and "annoy" are the text's words and are
-- not defined.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 24` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `administered to another person, or caused to be administered to or taken by another person, a poison or other destructive or noxious thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to injure that person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to aggrieve that person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to annoy that person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 24 (src:37)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 24`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND c's `administered to another person, or caused to be administered to or taken by another person, a poison or other destructive or noxious thing`
    AND (   c's `intended to injure that person`
         OR c's `intended to aggrieve that person`
         OR c's `intended to annoy that person`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 24 (src:37)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 24: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 24 (src:37)
